#

assertion  XSH.iswdigit.001
anchor     functions/iswdigit.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswdigit.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswdigit() returns non-zero for each character
           of the class digit as the locale definition lists it: the ten
           decimal digits.
test       t/001-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswdigit.002
anchor     functions/iswdigit.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswdigit.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswdigit() returns 0 for each of these
           characters, which the locale definition does not place in the
           class: the letters, the punctuation, the white-space characters and
           the controls.
test       t/002-non-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswdigit.003
anchor     functions/iswdigit.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswdigit.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       iswdigit(WEOF) is within the domain and returns 0, since WEOF is
           not a character of the class.
test       t/003-weof.c

assertion  XSH.iswdigit.004
anchor     functions/iswdigit.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswdigit.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       Each decimal digit is also an alnum and an xdigit character and is
           not an alpha character.
test       t/004-digit-relations.c

assertion  XSH.iswdigit.005
anchor     functions/iswdigit.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswdigit.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In a UTF-8 locale iswdigit() is non-zero for the ten digits and 0
           for every other ASCII-range character (the digit class has only
           those members in every locale).
note       Needs an installed multibyte UTF-8 locale (NOTINUSE otherwise);
           only ASCII-range characters are examined.
test       t/005-utf8-portable.c
